{% import "steps/_shared.en.jinja" as shared with context %}

{% macro resume_text(ref, full_context, completed_tasks) -%}
{% if ref %}Resume task: {{ ref }}.{% else %}Resume the task above.{% endif %} The recorded state and{% if completed_tasks %} completed sub-task results{% else %} conversation{% endif %} above are the inputs for this continuation.
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro resume(ctx) -%}
{% if ctx.resume_snapshot %}{{ resume_text(ctx.resume_snapshot.ref, true, ctx.resume_snapshot.completed_tasks) }}{% else %}{{ resume_text(ctx.task_ref if ctx.title else none, false, false) }}{% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro guidance(state) -%}
---
{{ shared.task_anchor(state.task_ref) }}

{% if state.plan_tasks %}{% if state.has_other_tasks %}## The overall plan (▶ = your current task; the rest are handled separately):
{% else %}## The overall plan (▶ = your current task):
{% endif %}{% for item in state.plan_tasks %}{{ "  " * item.depth }}- [{{ item.status }}] {% if item.current %}▶ {% endif %}{{ item.ref }}
{% endfor %}

{% endif %}{% if state.completed_tasks %}## Completed sub-task results (full results are in the conversation above):
{% for item in state.completed_tasks %}- [FINISHED] {{ item.ref }}
{% if item.result %}    → {{ item.result }}
{% endif %}{% endfor %}

{% endif %}{% if state.review_note %}## Note from the review of your previous attempt:
{{ state.review_note }}

{% endif %}{% if state.unattended %}This task is unattended; no user is available for a follow-up.{% endif %}{% if state.unattended_others %} Other tasks are handled separately.{% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro tool_instructions(ctx) -%}
{% set available = namespace(names=[]) %}
{% for section in ctx.capability_sections if section.kind == 'tool' %}
{% for item in section.ungrouped %}{% do available.names.append(item.name) %}{% endfor %}
{% for group in section.groups %}{% for item in group.entries %}{% do available.names.append(item.name) %}{% endfor %}{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}
Submit the actual final answer as normal message text. The observer receives it for task judgement.
{% if available.names %}Do not repeat a tool call with identical arguments.{% endif %}
{% if ask_user in available.names %}
- `{{ ask_user }}`: submit related questions together in one `questions` array. Each item has `question`; optional `options` contain `label`, `description` and `recommended`, and `multi_select` defaults to false. Omit `options` or use an empty array for free text; a free-text Other is always available. Execution pauses for the answers, then resumes with them as the tool result.
{% endif %}{% if switch_task in available.names %}
- `{{ switch_task }}`: call alone to replace a goal. Fill non-empty `title`, `description` and `task_prompt`. `target_task_id` identifies the OLD task: empty means current task; an ancestor ID replaces that whole branch, including the root for the whole goal. Supply `reason` for an ancestor. Siblings, unrelated tasks and terminal tasks cannot be targeted. The replacement occupies the same parent position; unfinished old tasks receive terminal review.
{% endif %}{% if delegate_task in available.names or delegate_plan in available.names %}
- Delegation suspends the current task until its sub-tasks finish. Fill `title` (at most 20 characters), `description` and `task_prompt` with the sub-task brief. Put orchestration choices only in `skill_name`, `use_subagent`, `subagent_template` and `inherit_memory`, not in that brief. To assign a skill, set `skill_name` to its exact listed name including the prefix; mentioning it in prose does not assign it. Skill logic runs in the assigned sub-task. `use_subagent` defaults to false; when true, `subagent_template` selects a listed sub-agent, or empty uses your own template. `inherit_memory` defaults to true. Attendance is inherited from the current task.
{% if delegate_task in available.names %}- `{{ delegate_task }}`: creates one sub-task. Use separate calls for independent tasks.
{% endif %}{% if delegate_plan in available.names %}- `{{ delegate_plan }}`: pass an ordered `tasks` array; each item uses the delegation fields above. A step starts only after its predecessor succeeds; failure cancels later steps.
{% endif %}{% endif %}{% if list_files in available.names or read_file in available.names or exec_script in available.names %}
- The assigned skill's resources belong to its provider, outside the workspace. Use the available skill-executor tools for those resources and filesystem tools for workspace files. Do not search the workspace for skill resources.
{% if list_files in available.names %}- `{{ list_files }}`: `pattern` is a glob within the skill (default `**/*`), with `limit` defaulting to 200.
{% endif %}{% if read_file in available.names %}- `{{ read_file }}`: `path` is relative to the assigned skill. Read by 1-based `offset` and line `limit` (defaults 1 and 2000), or by `char_offset` and `char_limit`; do not mix the two modes. Use the returned continuation hint to read the next page.
{% endif %}{% if exec_script in available.names %}- `{{ exec_script }}`: put the complete command, program and arguments in `command`, following the resource-access instructions supplied with the skill.
{% endif %}{% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro continuation(ctx) -%}
{% if ctx.guidance %}{{ guidance(ctx.guidance) }}{{ "\n\n" }}{% endif %}{% if ctx.needs_pointer %}{{ "\n\n" }}{{ shared.capability_pointer() }}{% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}

{% include "steps/_assemble.jinja" %}
